{"name":"Chocolate Oatmeal Cookie","hex":"#bb5544","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"},{"term":"oatmeal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Meal made from rolled or round oats.","A breakfast cereal made from rolled oats, cooked in milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light greyish brown colour, like that of oatmeal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oatmeal"},{"term":"cookie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, flat, baked good which is either crisp or soft but firm.","A sweet baked good (as in the previous sense) usually having chocolate chips, fruit, nuts, etc. baked into it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send a cookie to (a user, computer, etc.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cookie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oatmeal raisin cookie","blocks":[{"text":"An oatmeal raisin cookie is a type of drop cookie, featuring raisins throughout and oatmeal as the basis of the dough. Other typical ingredients include flour, sugar, eggs, salt, and spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Archway_Oatmeal_Raisin_cookies.JPG/330px-Archway_Oatmeal_Raisin_cookies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oatmeal_raisin_cookie","wikidata":"Q4320515"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","wikidata":"Q195"},{"title":"Oatmeal","blocks":[{"text":"Oatmeal is a preparation of oats that have been dehusked, steamed, and flattened, or a coarse flour of hulled oat grains (groats) that have either been milled (ground), rolled, or steel-cut. Ground oats are also called white oats. Steel-cut oats are known as coarse oatmeal, Irish oatmeal, or pinhead oats. Rolled oats were traditionally thick old-fashioned oats, but they can be made thinner or smaller and may be categorized as quick oatmeal or instant oatmeal depending on the cooking time required, which is determined by the size of the oats and the amount of precooking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Oatmeal.jpg/330px-Oatmeal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oatmeal","wikidata":"Q26883501"},{"title":"Cookie","blocks":[{"text":"A cookie is a sweet biscuit with high sugar and fat content. Cookie dough is softer than that used for other types of biscuit, and they are cooked longer at lower temperatures. The dough typically contains flour, sugar, egg, and some type of oil or fat. It may include other ingredients such as raisins, oats, chocolate chips, or nuts. Cookie texture varies from crisp and crunchy to soft and chewy, depending on the exact combination of ingredients and methods used to create them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg/330px-2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cookie","wikidata":"Q13266"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Oatmeal_Cookies_with_orange_zest%2C_golden_raisins%2C_and_chocolate_chips.jpg/500px-Oatmeal_Cookies_with_orange_zest%2C_go